<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4572" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλμῠρ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλμη</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>salt, briny,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>, and always in phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁ. ὕδωρ</span>
			<i>salt sea</i>-water, <i><span class="en">
				4.511
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					107
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				26
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάλασσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sapph.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					25.10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθ᾽ ἁ. ἅλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					53
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				76
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βένθεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					7.57
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποταμός,</span> of the Hellespont,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.35
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Prose, of
			taste, <i>salt,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γίνεται τὸ στόμα ἁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
				</span></i>
			<i>Acut.(Sp.)</i><i><span class="en">
				44
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψα ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					6.2.31
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Vict.</u>
				1.56
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἷμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					84a
				</span></i>
			 s.v.l.; of drinking-water, <i>brackish,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.26
			</span></i>; ofsoil, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				6.10.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Je.</u>
				17.6
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶρος</span> (insipid), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				596
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<i>bitter, distasteful,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γειτόνημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alcm.
					116
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				705a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκοή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					243d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					3.121e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλμυρὰ κλαίειν</span> weep
				<i>bitterly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				23.34
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλμυρὸν καταπτύσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cerc.
					19.37
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>piquant,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁ. καὶ δριμύ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.685e
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
